            <ArticleTitle>[Surgical decision-making in concomitant intrathoracic lesion of the aortic brachiocephalic branches and coronary arteries].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>113-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The work deals with analysing successful treatment of a total of eighteen patients presenting with intrathoracic lesions of the brachiocephalic branches of the aorta and coronary arteries. All the patients were operated on simultaneously, using different sequences of the interventions on the brachiocephalic and coronary arteries and different techniques of using artificial circulation. Cerebral stroke was revealed in two of the 18 patients (11%), with no coronary complications observed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
